diff --git a/dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md b/dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md
index 7b055fa..6617b89 100644
--- a/dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ The Switch 2 base dump reaches its title screen on the Mac. VideoToolbox decodes
 
 SDK 22.2.8, NVN API 231.40, with Nintendo's sead, agl and gsys. The three loaded modules are `main`, `subsdk0` (NintendoSDK_movie), and `sdk`. The NPDM declares 48 MiB of system resources. Startup requests a 6.20 GiB heap, which fits in the profile's 12 GiB reservation with the stack and alias regions. The registered build is the supplied base dump (`v0`).
 
+The low-memory defaults are on by default for this game, so the player does not have to turn them on in the launcher: `fps_target 30` (was 60), `render_scale_default 0.25` (was 0.667) and `potato_default on` (a new profile key; `game.py` emits `DM_GAME_POTATO_DEFAULT`, and `settings.tsv` uses it as the `DM_PRESET` default). A saved launcher choice or an env file that sets `DM_PRESET` still wins, and turning Potato off in the launcher is still one toggle. Not measured on an iPhone 15 Pro Max or an 8 GB Mac yet.
+
 ## Mac dry run
 
 Use the rewritten `patched_v0` and the original extracted `base/romfs`. Build the host with `make -C dm/host GAME=0400486024DEC000` and use the [Mac shader build](../../../docs/development.md#build-by-hand-mac). From the repository, set `DUMP` to the folder containing `base` and `WORK` to the build and run workspace beside it.
